public static int largestRectangleArea(int[] heights) {
    int n = heights.length;
    int[] left = new int[n];
    int[] right = new int[n];

    left[0] = 0;
    for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {
        int j = i - 1;
        while (j >= 0 && heights[i] > heights[j]) {
            j = left[j];
        }
        left[i] = j;
    }

    right[n - 1] = n;
    for (int i = n - 2; i >= 0; i--) {
        int j = i + 1;
        while (j < n && heights[i] > heights[j]) {
            j = right[j];
        }
        right[i] = j;
    }

    int maxArea = 0;
    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        maxArea = Math.max(maxArea, heights[i] * (right[i] - left[i] - 1));
    }

    return maxArea;
}
```
This solution uses two arrays `left` and `right` to store the indices of the previous larger bar to the left and right of each bar, respectively. The leftmost bar has a left index of 0 and the rightmost bar has a right index of `n`. The method then iterates over the bars and calculates the area of the largest rectangle that can be formed with each bar as the base. The maximum area is stored and returned at the end.

